{"kind":"assert","text":"CUT-R ruling on b871c4ac. R1 compares with no packet. It compares\nwith identifiers that R1 itself commits.\n\nIn R1, for each of Grow, Lending and Counter:\n- One committed file holds the identifiers that the pack path\n  gives for the canonical source at that head: the entry\n  definition, each other definition, and the presentation. It\n  holds no signature and no release digest.\n- The reproduction test prepares the package from its source and\n  compares each identifier with that file. A change of a source\n  that a packet holds then fails the test until the file changes\n  in a reviewed head.\nThe old Grow packet stays a fixture, and no test compares the new\nidentifiers with it.\n\nBefore I sign, I check that the packet I make at main carries the\nidentifiers of that file. A packet that differs is not pushed.\n\nIn R2 the same test gains one assertion for each package: the\ncommitted public packet carries the identifiers of the file, and\nits release and publisher equal the constants.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}